invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: a negative digit adds its multiple where it must subtract it,
  so the sum is wrong for every scalar whose digits hold one.
  bin/p384_equiv_test requires p384.c's verdict, and 1, on signatures
  of random scalars.

--- old
        p384_wide_mod_sub(term.y, zero, term.y, &p384_wide_modp);
--- new
        (void)zero;
